    {
      "id": "claim_7bf3f28cbea04232936f1c4b55d72ea0",
      "statement": "ZoneProcessor is configured with rows and cols (from ZoneSettings when provided by AppContext, else constructor defaults of 16/16); its self.zones dict and _rebuild_zone_ids() are vestigial — process_image() simply delegates to _process_ambilight() and returns a fresh dict each call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/zones.py#L11-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c837d1fdb17d9b2a61e73a9d574df558f5c55cc916c9c6ffc8d748f9e1859137:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_640784a5f85644d08a042e9aa682d287",
      "statement": "_process_ambilight() samples edge strips of width min(width // cols, height // 8) floored at 5 px: top and bottom edges are split into cols equal vertical strips, left and right edges into rows equal horizontal bands (64 zones at the 16x16 default), each zone being the np.mean of its strip cast to an int RGB tuple. Grayscale inputs are stacked to 3 channels, 4-channel inputs drop alpha, frames under 2x2 px return {}, and any exception is swallowed with a print plus {}. The sync loop's channel map covers only rows//2 left/right zones, so the lower-half left/right zones have no channel target and are dropped at update time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/sync.py#L100-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f7af4120f83d1ee3e0e1b4d73068a469fc70a068759d6305c7d2991d2d6cf986:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/zones.py#L36-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3000f2ef8e5edeabd2e2cef45182789024ada71749324433888dee49507a5a97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b1334d733f7e4d5cbeb1c7b443ba0920",
      "statement": "ColorAnalyzer is constructed in AppContext with brightness_scale and gamma taken from settings.sync. analyze_zone() first applies per-channel gamma (normalize to 0-1, raise to gamma with non-positive values falling back to 1.0, rescale to 0-255 ints), then computes brightness as max(r,g,b)/255*254*brightness_scale clamped to 1-254 — a max-component model chosen so blue/purple hues are not dimmer than green, since a luminance formula would weight green ~71.5% and blue ~7.2% — and finally converts via rgb_to_xy with the optional per-zone light_info.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/app_context.py#L40-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a91975edea2e52bdb1e6bbce1d4522abe46144e61b1042c03f1e862736475c84:"
        },
