          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/colors.py#L59-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:21e6d4662fd540572f448293c8b7f267984476f59568c08e01ecf3930ba614a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_662c6a66b1504dc8833c943282461234",
      "statement": "analyze_zones_batch() converts each zone RGB to (xy, brightness), consulting an optional light_info_map per zone to obtain light gamut data; the map is populated by HueBridge.refresh_devices() from the Hue API's per-light 'gamut' field, but the sync loop calls it without a map, so phosphor-gamut clamping is dormant in the shipped sync path — the mechanism exists in the public converter API but no call site wires light info into the pipeline.",
