    {
      "id": "claim_f7a61cdddf914d94bafdc81c5653f6e4",
      "statement": "rgb_to_xy() linearizes each sRGB channel with the standard piecewise transfer function (v <= 0.04045 -> v/12.92, else ((v+0.055)/1.055)^2.4), multiplies by the sRGB-to-XYZ D65 matrix, and returns x=X/(X+Y+Z), y=Y/(X+Y+Z); an all-black input (zero total) returns the fallback white point (0.3227, 0.3290).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lumux/utils/rgb_xy_converter.py#L4-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b22ab161a2c50aa7887fa1acfdc389614cb53025c9f4a119e82458a03c3eb58:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_439dffdc48d141c4b36007bbb79fe097",
      "statement": "When a gamut dict with red/green/blue phosphor {x,y} points is supplied (directly or via light_info['gamut'], each validated for x and y keys), _constrain_to_gamut() returns an in-triangle point unchanged (sign-test point-in-triangle), otherwise it projects to the nearest of the three triangle edges by computing the closest point on each segment (parameter clamped to 0..1) and taking the minimum-distance one.",
